            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I'm not sure these are really worth a table. And it's also slightly misleading. The `cython.py_*` names can equally be used in both, and it doesn't explain when or why users should write one or the other. I hope that's better explained by the paragraph that I added in https://github.com/cython/cython/commit/777ac6c2dbed5c4cbb3ab01b1a8b738dca045bc9",
            "commit_id": "e285591a3850dd9bffeb2e83c93db92d65a3e382",
